# A distribution update of a runtime dependency (unattended-upgrades) happens
# under a running daemon, and the version guard watches only zfsbackup and
# libzfseasy. When any of these directories changes, the postinst restarts the
# service if it is running (see "triggered" in debian/zfsbackup.postinst).
# noawait: the package that changed is not held back waiting for us.
#
# The list is every pure-Python or compiled module outside the standard library
# that the CLI, the daemon, its workers, the API and the remote client import,
# measured by importing them all and listing sys.modules on Debian 13 and Ubuntu
# 26.04, including the optional ones urllib3 and requests use when they are
# installed (brotli or brotlicffi, zstandard, simplejson; Suggests: or merely
# present on the host); python3-chardet and python3-charset-normalizer are both
# here because requests uses one on each distribution. dpkg matches a path component-wise
# (a directory covers what is under it; "name*" does not exist), so a module
# that is a single file or carries the interpreter and architecture in its name
# is listed by its exact path.
#
# NOT covered: shared libraries (libssl3 for ssl and cryptography, libffi,
# libsqlite3, libyaml): no path of ours would fire for them. needrestart
# (Recommends:) restarts a service whose mapped libraries were replaced.
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/flask
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/werkzeug
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/jinja2
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/itsdangerous
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/blinker
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/markupsafe
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/simple_websocket
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/wsproto
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/h11
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/websocket
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/sqlalchemy
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/alembic
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/click
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/requests
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/urllib3
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/cryptography
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/yaml
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/_yaml
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/mako
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/typing_extensions.py
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/greenlet
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/bcrypt
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/idna
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/certifi
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/chardet
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/charset_normalizer
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/brotlicffi
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/zstandard
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/simplejson
# Two packages ship modules whose file names carry the Python version and the
# architecture: python3-cffi-backend (_cffi_backend, cryptography's backend) and
# python3-brotli (_brotli, the one urllib3 uses when brotlicffi is absent). They
# are watched through a version-free path the same package ships, which every
# upgrade reinstalls: brotli.py, and python3-cffi-backend's doc directory (its
# only other path; copyright is kept even where path-exclude drops
# /usr/share/doc, as in Ubuntu's minimized images). Both checked to fire on
# Debian 13 and Ubuntu 26.04.
interest-noawait /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/brotli.py
interest-noawait /usr/share/doc/python3-cffi-backend
